      },
      "text": "Given a groupoid G, let us say an element A is idempotent if A⋆A is defined and A⋆A = A.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764636070899714,
        "y0": 0.7089958768902402,
        "x1": 0.7366657631070006,
        "y1": 0.7240908266317965
      },
      "text": "Lemma 2.3. An element A ∈ G is an idempotent if and only if A = g ⋆ g",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
